# testLatticeGeometry History

See `CONTRIBUTING.rst` for details of **required** info/format for each entry,
which **must** be added in reverse chronological order (newest at the top). It
must **not** be used as a substitute for writing good git commit messages!

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 2026-07-25 John Apostolakis (testLatGeom-V11-04-00)

New test using a geometry with a sphere at each lattice point, to compare memory
usage for geometry objects, in particular logical volumes and physical volumes.

- Used to compare footprint of setups with a large number of solid, logical and
  physical volumes.  Created to compare previous / existing code and new developments.

- Every lattice point own a separate logical volume by default (option for common LV.)

- Test script `run-lattice-benchmark.sh` compares serial vs tasking across a series
  of N x N x N lattice sizes

- Use the G4GeometryMemoryAdvisor to report memory usage.

